sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Tenant
    participant API as control-api
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant K as Kafka
    participant O as orchestrator
    participant P as proxmox-provider
    participant TF as Terraform
    participant PX as Proxmox

    Note over Tenant,PX: Every arrow below is asserted by pnpm run verify:terraform-runtime

    Tenant->>API: POST /instances + Idempotency-Key
    API->>API: validate — including SSH key structure
    Note right of API: A malformed key is refused here.<br/>Proxmox answers one with HTTP 500,<br/>which classifies as retryable.
    API->>DB: one transaction: instance, operation,<br/>IPv4 lease, audit entry, outbox row
    API-->>Tenant: 202 + operationId, statusUrl

    DB->>K: Debezium publishes the outbox row
    K->>O: provisioning.commands.v1, key = instance id
    O->>DB: claim with lease + fencing token
    O->>P: SubmitCreateInstance (context carries the fencing token)

    P->>DB: INSERT terraform.runs — before the apply starts
    Note right of P: SAFE-014. A worker that dies now<br/>leaves a reference a new worker polls,<br/>not a gap that invites a second apply.
    P->>TF: init + plan
    TF-->>P: plan JSON
    P->>P: gate: no-op / create / read / update only
    P-->>O: ACCEPTED + run id
    P->>TF: apply (the saved plan, never a fresh one)
    TF->>PX: clone 110, configure cloud-init, start
    PX-->>TF: VM 910xxx
    P->>DB: complete run, record workspace<br/>state serial + lineage

    loop until terminal
        O->>P: GetTask(run id)
        P->>DB: SELECT terraform.runs
    end

    O->>P: ApplyInstanceConfiguration
    P->>TF: plan — must be empty
    Note right of P: Convergence assertion, not a second write.
    O->>P: StartInstance
    O->>P: ObserveInstance
    P->>TF: apply -refresh-only
    P-->>O: exists, power, resources, ownership proven
    O->>DB: projection.instances — active

    Tenant->>API: GET /instances/{id}
    API-->>Tenant: active, observed state, leased address
    Note over Tenant,API: No provider resource id here.<br/>The VMID is restricted-operational.
